      "19275": {
        "comments": [
          {
            "creator": "kevinushey",
            "creation_time": "2026-11-02T03:45:48Z",
            "count": 0,
            "is_markdown": false,
            "text": "rWishart() R_Callocs two p-by-p work matrices and frees them only on the normal return path. Both of its argument errors are signalled in between ('scal' not positive-definite, and \"inconsistent degrees of freedom and dimension\" when df < p), so every failing call leaks 2 * p^2 doubles.\n\nReproducible example: attached as rwishart-leak-repro.R; it prints RSS growth per batch of 500 failing calls, which keeps climbing by up to about 310 MB per batch on both paths at p = 200 instead of levelling off.\n\nAnalysis: in src/library/stats/src/rWishart.c (r90825), the \"allocate early to avoid memory leaks\" comment covers the alloc3DArray only; the dpotrf check and std_rWishart_factor's df check both unwind past the R_Free at the end.\n\nProposed patch: attached as rwishart-leak.diff. It allocates the two buffers with R_alloc under vmaxget/vmaxset, so they are reclaimed on return and on error. With the patch, RSS stays flat on both paths and output for a given seed is unchanged.\n\nThe patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/331, where CI results can be seen.",
